    "created_at": "2016-10-03T09:28:53Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-10-03T09:28:53Z",
    "body": "FWIW, the reason I'm proposing this is because we have a number of places where two or more potentially independent processes need to take some \"in parallel\" action that can race with each other. Having a shared communication channel that can also keep some state around and run system calls is a way to solve that.\n\n> The idea of adding a placeholder object is much better for that.\n\nI don't really understand how that solves the communication issue.\n\n> We'll need some suitably made-up word.\n\nPerhaps something like a \"system event loop\" or \"user-agent event loop\"? (Instead of naming these, @jyasskin was suggesting we could instead introduce a concept that holds one of these, since you might also want to use one without a name, etc.)\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
