    "created_at": "2016-10-03T13:03:28Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-10-03T13:03:28Z",
    "body": "> I don't really understand how that solves the communication issue.\n\nCan you explain the communication issue in more detail then? Is it what you mentioned above in \"Communication is through some kind of message passing. I'm not sure how much we want to formalize that at the start.\", or something else? If it's that, could you translate that into some observable ambiguity in the spec?\n\nThe reason I ask is because the race condition is concrete and observable, and the solution proposed of using a placeholder value solves it elegantly. I'd like to understand what other concrete, observable problems we are hoping to solve here, especially if we're coming up with this entire new formalism which from what I understand doesn't match how browsers work at all.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
