    "created_at": "2016-10-03T13:40:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-10-03T13:40:20Z",
    "body": "I don't understand what placeholder value means or why browsers do not have something like what I propose today. If you have two processes that want to start a shared worker or write and read a cookie from disk, that needs to happen in an orderly fashion in some kind of manager thread. Otherwise the read can happen while the cookie is half written, or each process gets a unique worker despite it being shareable, etc.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
