    "created_at": "2016-10-05T13:28:47Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-10-05T13:28:47Z",
    "body": "No, this does not remove usage of \"atomically\", at least with the proposal as described in the OP. Atomically means that it cannot be interrupted or errored, whereas things in one named event loop can be interrupted by other named event loops interleaving between their steps (at least if they act anything like threads that browsers implement).\n",
