    "body": "@domenic it does, since the bits that need to be run atomically typically need to do so only within some limited scope, which would mean you'd queue them as set of steps in a thread and it would be fine. (That's effectively what you have to do to implement that today, which is why describing it like that would be a huge improvement over the status quo, which confuses everyone.)\n",
