    "created_at": "2016-10-05T16:57:38Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-10-05T16:57:38Z",
    "body": "My use case for this is https://github.com/WebBluetoothCG/web-bluetooth/issues/166. We could do it with an atomic test-and-set like @marcoscaceres suggested, which is similar to @domenic's placeholder objects, but using atomics is more error prone than taking locks or serializing things through dedicated threads.\n\nI'm not tied to the word \"thread\" here. The execution agent (a [term from C++](http://wg21.link/P0072R1)) that these things use is similar or identical to the one [Worklets](https://www.w3.org/TR/worklets-1/) use, so @bfgeek.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
