    "updated_at": "2017-09-12T17:30:46Z",
    "body": "I'm running into this too. My pattern is:\r\n\r\n>The add(*itemName*) method, when invoked, must return a new promise *promise* and run the following steps in parallel:\r\n>\r\n> * If *central list* contains *itemName*, reject *promise* with a TypeError and abort these steps.\r\n> * Do some stuff.\r\n> * Add *itemName* to *central list*.\r\n> * Resolve *promise*.\r\n\r\nTo avoid racing, I don't want two instances of these parallel steps to overlap.\r\n\r\nProviding an identifier for the thread could work. In my case I'm trying to keep adding to a particular list atomic, so passing that as the identifier would be ideal, as in:\r\n\r\n> Run the following steps in parallel, queued by the *central list*:\r\n\r\nCases that are more complicated than a single concept could generate and use UUIDs for thread identifiers.\r\n\r\n> Run the following steps in parallel, queued by the *someUUID*:",
